pra: 0202 - publish and honour the digitizer host-state contract

Provenance: T22 (ring65, work/boots.md T22 outcome, claim-0201 K4) resolved the
0201 fork: backboardd DOES configure through the event service - 40 setProperties
pushes (TouchDetectionMode x16, PreserveTimestamp x8, MotionEventRestricted x4,
GraphicsOrientation x2, ReportInterval/BatchInterval/DeviceOpenedByEventSystem/
LogLevel x2 each, QuantizationDPI/HIDSubinterfaceID x1) - and ZERO setElementValue
calls. The host-state handshake never started because this port advertises no
MultitouchHostStateKeys: backboardd's BKHIDUIHostStateDigitizerServiceWrapper only
pushes host state to services that publish the keys they honour (the vocabulary
is VERIFIED in the T21-era userland: WakeOnTapEnabled CoverGestureEnabled
WakeOnSwipeEnabled WakeOnLongPressEnabled WakeOnTapThroughEnabled
WakeOnSwipeThroughEnabled WakeOnLongPressThroughEnabled ScreenOn
DigitizerSurfaceCovered PocketTouchesExpected FaceTouchesExpected). The handoff
falsifier ("no setElementValue AND no setProperties line") was NOT hit, so 0202
is the lever. The exact private (page, usage) pairs could not be recovered
offline: the open-source IOHIDFamily usage tables carry no ScreenOn/HostState
usages (public digitizer table ends 0x55 in this tree, 0xA1 upstream), no donor
tree implements the contract, and the T21-era backboardd binary is gone from
/tmp. The accept net is therefore bounded (private digitizer-page usages) and
the NEXT ring names exactly what the advertisement pulls in.

BASE (derived, not assumed - claim-0201 K3): the old side is the post-0201 CI
build tree (/tmp/opencode/ci-tree-0201, buildtree.tgz == src byte-for-byte):
  iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp        = work/0202/SweetHID-pre0202.cpp
  iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/IOHIDEventService.h = the CI tree header
Round-trip proof: CI post-0201 files, patch -p1 -R --fuzz=0 of 0201 then
patch -p1 --fuzz=0 of 0201, cmp rc=0 against both bases. NOTE: the 0201 header's
framebuffer base derivation missed 0171's prague_gpu block; work/0201/
SweetFramebuffer-*0201.cpp must NOT be used as a base (claim-0201 K3). This
patch touches no framebuffer file.

WHAT CHANGES (four items, work/0202-design.md):
 1. SweetHIDTouch::start() publishes MultitouchHostStateKeys = OSArray of
    OSString [ScreenOn, DigitizerSurfaceCovered, PocketTouchesExpected] - exactly
    the keys we honour. WakeOnTapEnabled is NOT advertised: it implies a
    tap-to-wake delivery path that does not exist yet (0203). Also publishes
    SurfaceDimensions = {Width, Height} (IOFixed mm 16.16, the A5XELTE arm's
    68x121 - the arm that compiles on PRA) next to the existing raw numbers
    (kIOHIDSurfaceDimensionsKey/kIOHIDWidthKey/kIOHIDHeightKey,
    IOHIDEventServiceKeys.h:110/120/130).
 2. IOHIDEventService::setElementValue accepts private digitizer-page usages
    (page == kHIDPage_Digitizer && usage > 0x55, beyond the public table this
    tree knows): store in a fixed 8-entry table on the service, log the
    transition, return kIOReturnSuccess. Public usages and other pages keep the
    0201 refusal + log (we parse no report descriptors; no claimed capability
    we lack). setProperties honours the three advertised keys on the exercised
    channel: store as a read-back property + log the value; TouchDetectionMode
    (the most-pushed key) gets its value logged too.
 3. SweetHIDTouch::touch() sets kIOHIDEventFieldDigitizerWillUpdateMask and
    DidUpdateMask on every finger child (the fields actually written) and on
    the collection (its own fields | the union of the children's), so the
    parent's mask is nonzero whenever any child's is - backboardd's VERIFIED
    check "ignoring subevent with nonzero didUpdateMask (on parent event with
    zero didUpdateMask)" (@0xcd925 in the T21-era binary). will == did: the
    fields are written synchronously in the same call. The update-mask bits
    are kIOHIDDigitizerEventUpdate*Mask (IOHIDEventTypes.h:577-605); the fields
    exist in IOHIDDigitizerEventData (IOHIDEventStructDefs.h:376-377) and are
    already serialized, so the event size does not change.
 4. IOHIDEventService.h: the 8-entry HostStateEntry table (zeroed allocation =
    nothing set, the 0201 precedent).

Ring lines that prove the contract moved (next boot, ring66):
    SWEET HID: hoststate keys published (ScreenOn DigitizerSurfaceCovered
        PocketTouchesExpected)                       - once, at start()
    SWEET HID: SweetHIDTouch keyvalue ScreenOn = 1   - backboardd IS pushing
        host state through the advertised contract (any of the three keys)
    SWEET HID: SweetHIDTouch setElementValue page 0x.. usage 0x.. value 0x..
        -> accepted (was N set 0|1)                  - the element channel too
    SWEET HID: digitizer update masks set            - once, before first touch
    SWEET HID: SweetHIDTouch keyvalue TouchDetectionMode = N  - the x16 key's
        values, invisible before

FALSIFIER: a boot with the publication line but NO keyvalue/host-state line and
NO accepted element write means backboardd reads the advertisement but still
does not push - the gate is then upstream (SpringBoard's sensor-mode assertion,
0203's display-power honesty) and the tracev3 route-log decode
(digitizer-gate-2026-11-22.md section 5: digitizer:%llX - display: @0xcde28 with
our senderID, contacts now @0xcdb2f) is the next step, not more host-state work.
A boot WITHOUT the publication line means this patch was skipped (the marker
asserts below catch that in CI). Touch-from-boot with NO synthetic key is the
deliverable test AFTER this lands; the keys stay on until then.

